# Build Artifacts
publish/
# Anchored to the repo root on purpose. Unanchored, `PublishProfiles/` also matches the
# TRACKED IdleLauncherTray/Properties/PublishProfiles/*.pubxml that the release workflow
# depends on. That is inert while the file is in the index, but a `git rm --cached` would
# make it silently un-re-addable without -f.
/PublishProfiles/
# Release workflow staging directory (release.yml builds the zip from here).
stage/
# `dotnet test` writes .trx and coverage here. Added with the first test project in v2.5.0 --
# before that there was no test output to ignore, which is why it was missing.
TestResults/

# Logs
*.log
logs/

# Credentials and signing material
# Nothing here has ever been committed -- this is a guard, not a cleanup. The realistic risk
# on a PUBLIC repo is a code-signing cert dropped next to the csproj for a one-off signed
# build, which is exactly the kind of file that gets swept up by a careless `git add -A`.
# `*.user` in the Visual Studio block above already covers *.pubxml.user by accident; these
# are deliberate. Verified with `git check-ignore -v` (each pattern matches, none shadows a
# tracked file) before being committed.
*.pfx
*.p12
*.snk
*.pem
*.key
.env
.env.*
secrets.json
appsettings.*.local.json

